WEBVTT

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:03.910
<i>Miracles.</i>

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:11.230
<i>Unexpected events which occasionally remind us
that reality is stranger than fiction.</i>

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.220
<i>They are especially frequent on Christmas Eve.</i>

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.320
<i>Maren joined the band
towards the end of autumn.</i>

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.380
<i>Fascinated by his skills,
and probably also by his good looks,</i>

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:00.760
<i>a whole bunch of girls joined with him.</i>

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.680
<i>Even as winter break began
and Christmas Eve rolled around,</i>

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:08.080
<i>we continued to practise.</i>

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:15.830
Brr!

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:22.360
Nice catch!

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:24.980
It's freezing up here!

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:26.950
Do something about this, Haruta.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:28.460
I can't, Chika-chan.

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:32.250
The choir's got dibs on the music room,
and the gym is overrun by sports teams.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:35.600
Can't we rent out a community centre or studio?

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:36.800
We don't have the budget.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:40.130
So the rooftop's our stage, huh?

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:43.260
If you've got pocket money to burn, please donate!

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:48.240
We're short on practice venues,
budget, and members.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:52.890
Let's rehearse one more time.
We can call it a day after that.

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:07.160
Wait...

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.830
H-Haruta's sister?!

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:14.870
Thank you for taking such good care of Haruta.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.150
Kamijou... Minami-san?

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:24.640
In summer haiku terms, the characters
for "southern wind" are read as "Minami".

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.390
It's a wonderful name.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:28.890
Oh, I'm Katagiri Keisuke, the president.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:30.940
Might you be a fashion model?

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:31.990
I'm an architect.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:32.810
Are you married?

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:34.060
What is <i>wrong</i> with you?

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:38.360
Long time no see, Chika-chan.
It's been ten years, has it?

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.810
I guess! How are Tsugumi-san
and Fuyuna-san doing?

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:43.940
Who are they?

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:46.660
The younger two of Haruta's older sisters.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:51.320
Tsugumi became an illustrator who
keeps drawing these bizarre pictures,

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:55.930
while Fuyuna cracks her patients'
bones as a chiropractor.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:58.380
Wow, Kamijou-kun. You have three sisters?

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:00.300
As much as it pains me, yes.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.240
<i>I'm</i> the one who's pained here.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.550
You're a disgrace!

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:16.610
Please don't tell me you live here.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:17.900
Oh, Kamijou-kun.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:20.000
We cleaned your place while we were at it.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.530
Here, have some eggs.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.070
Thanks as always!

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:26.480
Why are you the biology club's pet now?
What are you, a chicken?!

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:27.950
Calm down, Chika-chan!

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.480
I had no choice.

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.640
My apartment complex got demolished.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:33.120
Were you thrown out without notice?

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:37.290
Nah. I just thought they'd pay for the move
if I held out as long as possible.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.610
It didn't work, though.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:41.130
Your phone's been disconnected too, hasn't it?

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.670
That's why I had to come all the way here.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:46.110
Why won't you go home?

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:47.090
Oh, right.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:49.510
That place is hell.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.570
That's not a nice thing to say.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:55.030
They make me pose nude for sketches
and use me for chiropractic experiments!

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:59.190
I see he can't say no to his sisters.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:02.320
Well, it's not like I don't
understand how you feel.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:05.110
So I've decided to help pay for the move.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.240
We're going to find you
an apartment today, Haruta.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.410
Now?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.070
On Christmas Eve?

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:11.780
That doesn't sound like a good idea.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:13.680
And what if you don't find one today?

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.210
I'm not coming back home!

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.040
If I can't stay here,
I'll go live under a bridge!

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.170
Do you want me to dump
you in the river again?

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:24.500
If it's just for a little while,
you can stay with me.

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:25.840
No!

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:28.800
In that case, the apartment hunting
can wait until the new yea—

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.250
Absolutely not!
We can't cause trouble for Sensei!

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:33.510
I'll do everything in my power
to find him a place!

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.600
So that Haruta can eat his
Christmas cake in a new home!

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:40.100
It's all good. I'll eat it at Sensei's place—

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.270
The rest of you will help too, right?

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:46.920
Sorry, but I have to head home.
I've got dinner plans with my parents.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.990
I've got work too, unfortunately.

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.510
Then let's do what we can by ourselves!

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:52.570
By ourselves?!

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:57.540
You're a lucky guy, Haruta.
Not everyone has such a caring childhood friend.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:02.990
I called one of my father's friends
who works at a real estate agency.

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:04.000
Thanks!

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:06.340
Get in.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:08.130
I'll walk.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:10.050
There's no time for that!

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:14.000
You never realise the
important things, Chika-chan.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:14.720
Off we go.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:23.480
Um, Minami-san, aren't we going a bit too fast?

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:25.330
Don't talk! You'll bite your tongue!

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.360
Go straight down this road.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:34.410
My sister has this pointless habit
of turning at every intersection.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.560
What?!

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:47.920
The budget is 20,000 yen. Not one yen more.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:51.630
It might be hard to find a place within
walking distance from school with that budget.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:55.180
Found one!

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:58.470
The rent's only 4,000 yen!
And it's close to school!

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:01.360
Uh, that's a parking lot.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:02.520
How about this, then?

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.320
You can handle a two-and-a-half-hour
walk to and from school, right?

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.340
That's a trek, not a walk!

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:08.960
Is it okay if it doesn't have a bath?

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:10.030
A-okay!

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:13.070
80-year-old building, north-facing
4.5 tatami-size room, no bath,

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:16.700
shared toilets, and the rent is 9,000 yen.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:20.700
I hear apartments like these have
edible mushrooms growing in the closets.

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.850
You read too much manga, Nee-san!

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:23.790
What about this one?

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:26.450
Rent is 20,000 yen, 1BK apartment
with wooden flooring.

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:28.970
The kitchen's 2.5 tatami mats, and the room's 9.

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:30.490
It even has a toilet and bath.

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:32.870
And it's soundproofed!

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:34.720
You could practise the horn there!

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:35.890
Soundproofed?

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:39.360
You're right.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:44.180
The building's 40 years old,
but it underwent major renovations in 1982.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:46.160
This place sounds too good to be true.

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:50.480
That apartment's a bit problematic.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:52.060
Is it next to a graveyard or something?

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:54.280
No, an empty lot.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:57.030
Next to an empty lot, yet soundproofed...

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:58.930
All right. We're going with that.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:07:59.530
Um...

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:03.390
Do you have a detailed
floor plan or some blueprints?

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:04.460
I do, yes.

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:08.880
The ground and first floors have two each.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.640
The landlord lives on the second floor.

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:13.800
Huh? But it says here that there are six rooms.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.180
You're right.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.440
Maybe the landlord listed it wrong?

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:19.470
Would they really make
such a major mistake?

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:22.560
So, how exactly is this place problematic?

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:26.470
The thing is, the previous landlord
passed away two months ago.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:27.800
Oh, so it's a crime scene?

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:32.230
No, no. He died of old age at the hospital.

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:35.730
But people have been complaining
about this place for ages.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:36.650
Complaining?

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:40.490
Every tenant has ended up leaving.

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:43.660
There's a strange rumour about the place.

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:57.400
The landlord's apartment
was on the second floor, right?

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:00.350
An elderly person would've had
real trouble getting up there.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:08.310
Say.

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:11.600
What's wrong, Narushima-san?

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:14.480
I feel some kind of presence.

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:16.690
Don't you sense anything?

00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:17.730
Not really.

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.250
Gotcha.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:22.990
Jeez!

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:26.850
He said that the former landlord's
nephew lives here now.

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:30.420
His nephew inherited the building?

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:33.470
Yes?

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:35.880
Here you are.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.390
Thank you.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:39.800
Something smells nice!

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:45.810
My wife is making some
Christmas cake and roast chicken.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:48.390
Though it might be too much
for just the two of us.

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:52.930
Would you like to try some?

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:54.290
Can I?!

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:55.320
Hey, Haruta!

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:58.490
Good thing I brought my own chopsticks.

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:03.240
Sorry to drop by so suddenly.

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:06.410
The real estate agent asked us
to negotiate directly with you.

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:10.400
Actually, we've decided to sell this place.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:12.960
Haruta here isn't scared of ghosts.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:16.450
Oh, so you already know.

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:19.300
What kind of ghost is it?

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:27.380
A playful ghost who has three hairs on his head
and eats twenty bowls of rice at once?

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:28.960
If so, he's scared of dogs.

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:30.300
Nee-san...

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:33.640
Rumour has it that a creepy monk's
ghost haunts this place.

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:34.790
Monk?

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:36.520
Have you seen it too?

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:39.600
No, not at all.

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:45.390
But the people who lived here said that
late every night, they heard a monk's staff...

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:50.960
ringing throughout the building.

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:54.240
Any idea when that started?

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:57.000
After the renovations, apparently.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:00.590
That was in 1982, right?

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:01.510
Yes.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:05.440
This building has a double-wall
construction that makes it soundproof,

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:07.930
so it shouldn't be possible
to hear any outside noise.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:10.680
Yeah, that much is clear
from the window frames.

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:15.230
Oh, but the lack of tenants
isn't the only reason we're selling.

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:16.150
Is it the inheritance tax?

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:18.170
Yes.

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:24.000
Embarrassing as it may be,
I can't pay it without selling.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:27.470
How did you end up inheriting this place?

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:30.200
My uncle is survived by a son and daughter.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:39.470
But in his will, he left me this building and all
of its furniture, supplies, and precious metals.

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:43.380
He wrote his will on the original floor plan?

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:46.520
Yes. My uncle was a wealthy man,

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:49.550
but this building doesn't have
anything particularly of value.

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:50.830
Just a whole lot of tax.

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:55.560
Is that why his children agreed to let you inherit it?

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:56.820
That's right.

00:11:57.510 --> 00:12:01.150
Maybe my uncle wanted to cause me trouble.

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:05.990
He was a playful man who loved pranks.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:09.580
His family and relatives
considered him an annoyance.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:14.250
I loved him, though.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:17.980
I spent a lot of time laughing with him.

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:24.050
But once I grew up, life got harder.

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:27.160
I was a guarantor for a friend
who saddled me with debt.

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:29.200
The company I worked for went bankrupt.

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:32.770
And when I started my own,
my partner took the capital and ran.

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:34.040
So one day...

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:43.190
Quit doing these stupid things already!

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:46.570
My life isn't as carefree as yours!

00:12:47.020 --> 00:12:51.490
I ended up taking it out on him,
and we had been estranged ever since.

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:54.910
I finally found a full-time
job not too long ago,

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.460
got married, and was blessed with a baby.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:03.500
And I inherited this building,
but I don't have the money to pay the tax.

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:07.270
I don't even know if I can sell it off,
because of the whole ghost business.

00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:10.300
You've had it rough.

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:14.520
Was this building the only thing he left you?

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:15.890
Yes.

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:18.850
Actually, there was one more thing.

00:13:20.510 --> 00:13:22.270
I got this along with the blueprints.

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:24.900
Apparently it's the key to the sixth room.

00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:28.280
Doesn't this building
only have five apartments?

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:29.600
That's right.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:32.950
This is just a prank meant to cause me trouble.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:34.700
All because I snapped at him that day.

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:39.000
Haruta, can't you at least
solve the ghost mystery?

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.310
Why me?

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:41.920
They fed you!

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.430
Exorcise it right now!

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:45.130
I can't! And it'd be pointless, anyway!

00:13:46.330 --> 00:13:48.470
Sorry we can't be of any help.

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:50.930
It's fine.

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:52.550
I appreciate the thought.

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:02.810
It's vernacular modernism.

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:16.080
In our industry, we have this category
called vernacular architecture.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.750
Vernacular?

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:20.740
Simply put, it refers to buildings
not built by architects.

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:24.880
They're built by locals,
in line with local features and traditions.

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:28.440
It includes stuff like stilt houses
and Kyoto's traditional homes—

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:31.050
architecture that's rooted
in local, everyday life.

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:32.930
Vernacular, huh?

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:35.940
What was that apartment building's
supernatural phenomenon?

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:39.370
They say the ghost of a monk
shows up in the dead of night.

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:40.880
Be more specific.

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:44.230
They hear a staff going ring-ring.

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:47.000
That's what you call vernacular.

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:49.520
Your thinking is influenced by local tradition.

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:51.500
Let's say you do hear that sound.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:53.930
Why would you assume it's a monk's staff?

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:56.830
Thank you.

00:14:56.830 --> 00:15:00.020
That was a ring-ring sound, too.

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:04.070
Right. People just jumped to conclusions
and assumed that it was a monk's staff.

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:08.380
So thinking the place is haunted
is vernacular by itself?

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:10.630
Something's not right.

00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:16.600
Thank you!

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:19.920
Oh, well. The apartment search
will have to wait until tomorrow.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:22.080
I'll go stay with Kusakabe-sensei, then.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:26.420
I would absolutely love to
take him up on his offer—

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:28.150
I mean, it'd be rude to turn him down.

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:30.740
Why are you so fixated on staying with him?

00:15:32.810 --> 00:15:36.500
Um, Haruta really looks up to Kusakabe-sensei.

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:40.910
He's an amazing person who once came runner-up
at the Tokyo international music competition!

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:44.710
Kamijou-kun, Maren just invited us over for dinner.

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:47.870
He says you can stay the night, too.

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:48.420
All right!

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:53.510
So sorry to cause you all
this trouble on Christmas Eve.

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:57.780
Don't worry!
Kamijou-kun has helped us out a lot!

00:15:57.780 --> 00:16:00.310
We'd love for you to
celebrate Christmas with us!

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:04.400
I'm sorry, but it seems I already
have dinner waiting at home.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:08.480
I only came with Haruta because
his phone's disconnected, too.

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:11.650
Nobody asked, Chika-chan.

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:13.080
How shameless...

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:15.170
Don't hold back. Eat as much as you want.

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:17.240
We just ordered some pizza, too.

00:16:18.130 --> 00:16:19.370
Oh, looks like it's here.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.060
I'll get it.

00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:22.920
Thank you. Here you go.

00:16:24.070 --> 00:16:25.710
Oh, let me pick that up for you.

00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:28.860
Too bad you couldn't find a new apartment.

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:31.960
Actually, we found a really nice one,
but it's got baggage attached.

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:33.130
Oh? What kind?

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:35.930
One of these shows up!

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:37.100
What's that?

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:39.180
A meerkat.

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:40.890
Maren.

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:42.440
What is it?

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:45.920
I want you to look up what happened in 1982.

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:46.980
What's gotten into you?

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:51.900
A really absurd thought just crossed my mind.

00:16:52.310 --> 00:16:54.700
1982...

00:17:01.110 --> 00:17:02.280
Let's go, guys.

00:17:03.260 --> 00:17:04.200
Where to?

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:05.200
That apartment complex.

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:06.810
What are you talking about?

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:08.720
You should come too, Nee-san.

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:11.130
It's possible this will remain
a mere fantasy of mine,

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:16.120
but you might just get to see
the most absurd Christmas miracle ever!

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:21.000
You're a Class 1 architect.
Don't you want to see it?

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:22.050
See what?

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:25.640
The ultimate vernacular modernism!

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:28.440
What's all this about?

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:31.670
You're not supposed to use the band's
mailing list for personal reasons.

00:17:31.670 --> 00:17:34.270
What's this miracle we just gotta see?

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:35.440
What's going to happen?

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:37.110
O-Oh, Minami-san!

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:38.200
Good evening.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:40.080
It's a beautiful night, isn't it?

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:42.030
Amano-san agreed to join us too.

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.700
What's this I hear about a miracle?

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:46.400
Kusakabe-sensei?!

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:48.480
You called him too, Haruta?

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:52.090
I just thought he might be interested.

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:53.660
Besides, he's our advisor.

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:54.880
Good job!

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:57.850
I can't think of it as just a coincidence.

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:00.220
A soundproof double-wall construction,

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:03.390
the non-existent sixth room and its key,

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:07.560
the strange sound that people
started hearing after the renovation,

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:09.680
and the will written on the blueprints.

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:12.170
What do you mean?

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:14.400
You'll find out soon enough.

00:18:27.050 --> 00:18:28.660
Sorry to drop by so late.

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:30.120
Don't be.

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:35.460
If I'm on the right track,
you might not need to sell this building.

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:39.380
Here.

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:42.050
I found it. There's no doubt about it.

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:44.100
Give it a shot, Nee-san.

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:44.840
Here goes.

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:49.580
What was that sound?

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:50.980
The ghost of a monk?

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:57.400
Wow. Maybe it's reached
the second floor already.

00:18:58.010 --> 00:19:01.820
Amano-san, your uncle left you
that floor plan for a reason.

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:05.740
It's both a will and a treasure map.

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:07.450
Treasure map?

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:10.820
Get the key to the sixth room, Amano-san.

00:19:10.820 --> 00:19:13.370
There must be a keyhole somewhere!

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:24.510
Could this be it, Haruta?

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:29.390
All yours, Amano-san.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:30.630
Okay...

00:19:54.180 --> 00:19:55.520
What the hell?

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:57.720
500 yen coins?

00:19:57.720 --> 00:19:59.040
Fantastic!

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:03.840
It's a Christmas miracle.

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:12.230
The sixth room referred to the
gap between the two walls,

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:14.980
which was filled with 500 yen coins.

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:20.270
This entire apartment building
was basically a piggy bank for them.

00:20:20.270 --> 00:20:25.290
So what did you find out when
you had Maren look up 1982?

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:28.200
It was the year the 500 yen coin was issued.

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:33.690
Maybe that was what set off this grand plan.

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:36.370
Wait, so that ringing sound earlier...

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:40.150
It was the sound made by a 500 yen coin
dropped from the second floor.

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:44.550
So that's what the "ghost" really was.

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:47.840
Just how much money does this add up to?

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:49.220
Stop that!

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:51.620
Considering the height of the wall,

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:56.000
it should have enough to make it
well worth inheriting the building.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:00.560
But why would he do this?

00:21:00.560 --> 00:21:04.760
He probably thought it'd be fun
if his house was one big piggy bank.

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:05.400
That,

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:08.910
and he probably wanted to
surprise Amano-san too.

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:17.590
This is so stupid, Uncle.

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:22.000
All done moving!

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:25.380
I'm glad that you found
such a nice place, Kamijou-kun.

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:27.350
Thanks, everyone.

00:21:27.350 --> 00:21:30.070
You didn't have much stuff, so it was easy.

00:21:30.070 --> 00:21:31.300
Good work, kids.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:34.350
I brought soba. Convenience store soba, but hey.

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:36.600
Thank you, Minami-san!

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:37.970
Let's eat!

00:21:37.970 --> 00:21:40.250
Oh, and here.

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:42.210
You'd better be grateful.

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:50.160
It's a video of a contest Kusakabe-sensei
participated in while studying abroad.

00:21:50.670 --> 00:21:52.060
He has such amazing presence.

00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:52.870
Yeah.

00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:57.960
Why would he teach music at our school?

00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:33.300
Only the colour of the sky is different, huh?

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:35.410
An invention like that would make
Alexander Graham Bell cry!

00:23:35.410 --> 00:23:36.720
There's still time.

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:40.400
He said he saw the elephant's breath.
